ne Utilities still priced a C$1.1B bond comfortably. Its 2027 capex is planned up 12%, and it looks financeable through bonds.\n\n**Equity: weak**\n- Pellham Power withdrew its C$2.4B equity offering after investor demand fell short.\n- Two other utility share offerings were cut back in size, and the Q3 credit report calls equity markets \"less receptive\".\n\n**Pellham is the problem case**\n- Its 2027 capex was planned up 18%, and it is the largest single buyer of grid equipment in Caldria.\n- It is cutting 2027 transformer orders by about 40% and deferring two substation programmes \"until financing improves\".\n- Stronger issuers like Norvane can rely on bonds, but larger or weaker ones like Pellham can't count on equity and will cut or defer spending.\n\n**What the sources don't show**\n- There is no leverage, ratings or balance-sheet data, so I can't tell whether Pellham's debt capacity is exhausted or whether it simply didn't try a bond issue.\n- Norvane's equity plans are not covered.\n- Nothing shows whether equity could reopen in 2027.\n- The evidence rests on only three documents, so treat this as a directional view.\n\nThe detailed answers are in n5.r1 (debt) and n6.r1 (equity).","ttft_ms":1713,"type":"result","duration_ms":27820,"uuid":"2e6e7e74-8b15-4f83-905e-f54412488568","ttft_stream_ms":1109,"time_to_request_ms":168,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":15,"system_prompt":15,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":2,"input_attachments":22,"input_hooks":8,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":31,"tool_pool_refresh":2,"init_message":9,"init_frame_send":6,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":7,"message_prep":0,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":6,"request_announcements":17,"query_setup":1,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":12,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":4,"request_build":7},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":61,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":88,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib